You become a co-owner of a real company. {{1}}
It is not backed by a real company with factories, employees and profits. {{2}}
A dividend may be distributed if a profit is made. {{3}}
The price is determined by supply and demand on a marketplace. {{4}}
Fluctuations are often extreme – the price can jump by several tens of per cent within weeks. {{5}}
The value can fall – a loss is possible. {{6}}
You may vote at the annual general meeting. {{7}}
It is purely digital money that operates without a government, central bank or banks. {{8}}
In an extreme case, a total loss is possible. {{9}}
